 ### [Mask Projection Culling](6836-mask-projection-culling.md)
-Mask Projection Culling is a visibility-based mesh filtering technique that removes faces and vertices not consistently observed across multiple camera poses by projecting points into camera space and comparing their depth against rendered depth maps or binary masks. It differs from simple adjacency culling by using actual camera views to determine visibility, allowing it to cull geometry that is occluded by other objects in the scene rather than just adjacent voxels. It differs from [Face Coverage Mask Culling](3397-face-coverage-mask-culling.md) by operating on the final mesh geometry (vertices/faces) rather than pre-computing coverage masks during voxel traversal.
